Put L3-only interfaces into the flowtable

fw4 builds the flowtable device list from each zone's related_physdevs,
which is fed only from a network's physdev, and physdev is set from the
ubus network.interface field "device" with no fallback:

	device:  ifc.l3_device ?? ifc.device,
	physdev: ifc.device,

An interface whose protocol never creates an L2 device reports only
l3_device. ModemManager is the case here: `ubus call network.interface
dump` shows the wwan interface with "l3_device": "wwan0" and no "device"
field at all, so physdev is undefined, the guard at the push site skips
it, and wwan0 silently never enters the flowtable.

The result is a flowtable holding only the LAN side. Flow offload needs
both directions' devices, so with a 5G modem as WAN the generated
flowtable is:

	devices = { "br-lan", "eth0" }

and no LAN-to-internet flow can ever be offloaded. Nothing reports this;
the flowtable exists and looks healthy.

Fall back to l3_device when device is absent. This only ever adds
devices that previously resolved to nothing - where "device" exists it
still wins, so PPPoE and VLAN setups keep resolving to their lower
device exactly as before. physdev is read in only two places, both
inside the flowtable device resolution, so nothing else changes.

--- a/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
@@ -619,7 +619,7 @@
 				let net = {
 					up: ifc.up,
 					device: ifc.l3_device ?? ifc.device,
-					physdev: ifc.device,
+					physdev: ifc.device ?? ifc.l3_device,
 					zone: ifc.data?.zone
 				};
 
